#############

# KMTNet script by Vedant Chandra to observe WD+WD binaries. 
# Co-Is: Yuan-Sen Ting, Hsiang-Chih Hwang, Kareem El-Badry, J.J Hermes

##########################################
# Target 1: ZTF J0347−1802, Gaia EDR3 5107322396824711680
# Hermes WD with transiting debris, G = 17.4
# Measuring transits, recurrence period
##########################################

# Start the observations once the target rises to airmass less than 2.

# PID LABEL   RA    DEC   COPT  IMGTYP  OBJECT    FILTER EXPTIME  UTOBS UTTOL

  WDTD  target1 03:47:03.36   -18:02:53.70  - OBJECT  J0347m1802  V 60 - -

+ostart 1

# Repeat the observations until the object falls to airmass less that 2, or twilight.
# Repeat on two consecutive or near-consecutive nights
# The target is at high airmass all night in November, so it should be observed for a total of 
# around 12 hours across 2 nights. If this is cut short due to weather, then kindly repeat the observations on 
# another night until the total monitored time is around 12 hours. 

##########################################
# Target 2: Gaia EDR3 3076962575704962176
# Short period WD+WD with Gemini Follow-up, G = 17.9
# Monitoring for eclipses/ellipsoidal
##########################################

# Start the observations once the target rises to airmass less than 2.  

# PID	LABEL 	RA		DEC		COPT	IMGTYP	OBJECT		FILTER EXPTIME	UTOBS	UTTOL

  WDWD	target2	08:31:07.92 +00:13:31.37	-	OBJECT	J0831p0013	V	60	-	-

+ostart 3

# Repeat the observations until the object falls to airmass less that 2, or twilight. 

